checks_run.procedure:
Confirm the frozen candidate:
- check the assignment's sha256;
- recompute the candidate ID in the repository, and in the disposable clone after the runs with the probe copy moved out;
- confirm that HEAD is the freeze commit on top of source_commit and that only delivery records changed since;
- run the DG1 historical validation.

On a fresh disposable stack (PG16 UTF8 + API, synthetic seed), create transformations and walk Diagnose→Define→Design through the API as dev.lead, dev.office and dev.admin. Cover:
- the modes and the B0018 roles;
- the B0023 gate names and sequential G1→G2→G3, with out-of-sequence submissions refused;
- T01 with six dimensions and H/M/L confidence, the six B0029 workstreams and the ten B0056 dimensions;
- the 14-field charter with versions, the composed four-part B0037 thesis (incomplete when a part is blank or invisible-only), and the five B0039-B0043 scope checks;
- one current North Star, the 3-5 outcome warning, the good-outcome test, and guardrails (G2 blocked at zero);
- the T02 target date;
- the TOM canvas (ten boxes, B0062 prompts; ready needs a target and an owner), and G3 blocked until the gap matrix, capability gaps and future journeys exist;
- live G1, G2 and G3 decisions;
- Arabic charter text with RLM/ALM accepted verbatim, and invisible-only values refused (validation.blank) across fields.

Through the API, exercise:
- T04 (B0065) and T03 (B0058);
- the capability heatmap linked to a T03 gap;
- a journey with a decimal cycle time and a pain point linked to a T01 row;
- a TOM workshop item converted into a T04 decision (owner required);
- the per-dimension view.

Re-run my earlier-round API regression probes on the round-12 candidate:
- r11-delta-api (D-071: keep-alive upload, 413 oversized, SPA deep links, unknown API 404);
- r10-delta-api (D-070: content types);
- regress-d069-api (evidence binary round trip, media-type refusals);
- regress-d068-api (UTF-8 body and query decoding);
- regress-d067-api (lone surrogates);
- regress-d066-api (NUL and placeholder-only).

Browser walk in EN and AR of the Diagnose, Define, Design, Gates, G1 detail and Evidence pages of one synthetic transformation. Check:
- html dir/lang;
- that each page renders;
- the B0023 gate names (EN) and the Arabic names (AR);
- that no text claims PMI certification or official Mobily branding, and that no page names DG0-DG7;
- that the provisional wordmark is present.

New probe for the FE9 sweep, which moved the StepsEditor row key out of its state updater (REQ-PB-025). In Chromium, in EN and AR:
- create a synthetic process map through the API;
- in Design, open its steps and pain points, then Edit steps;
- add three steps (Arabic names with RLM in AR), and give step 2 a cycle time of 1.5 days;
- move step 3 up, save, and read the journey back through the API.

checks_run.actual:
The source texts match the live outputs verbatim: the B0018 roles, the B0023 gate names and questions, the six B0029 workstreams, the ten B0056 dimensions, the B0062 prompts, the five B0039-B0043 checks and the B0009 How texts. T01 is Dimension / Current state / Evidence/baseline / Root cause / Impact / Confidence H/M/L, seeded with six dimensions. T02 adds a target date and a leading indicator. T03 has six columns. T04 has seven, with generated D-NN codes and Open by default.
The D-072 product diff covers 19 files:
- evidence routes/store and platform hooks (three-phase upload; the central incomplete-body 400);
- the db pool bounds;
- RecordForm, which reports onValuesChange from an effect instead of inside the setValues updater (same timing semantics: never for the initial values);
- JourneysSection, where the step key is generated before setSteps (same data);
- tests and the warning guard.
No file under i18n, migrations, seeds, docs/source or the gate/criteria/transformation modules changed. No methodology text, gate criterion, sequence or register column changed. ADR-0007 §5b and the ops docs gained the 503 note.
Observation (no finding): on a fresh transformation the gate card shows G3 '1 of 5' complete because g3.design_decisions is a pure prohibition ('no open design decision without an owner'). This is documented in criteria.ts, unchanged since earlier rounds, and does not let G3 pass, which still needs the TOM, gap matrix, capability gaps and future journeys (B0023 'Target Operating Model, capability gaps, future journeys').

